    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs with «sig»",
     "texto": [
      "Many verbs take a reflexive pronoun, like «wash yourself» in English:\n\n- vaske **sig** = to wash oneself\n- barbere **sig** = to shave\n- sætte **sig** = to sit down\n- rejse **sig** = to stand up\n- kede **sig** = to get bored\n- skynde **sig** = to hurry\n- gifte **sig** = to get married\n\n**sig** is for him, her or them when it's the same as the subject: Nina slog **sig** (she hurt herself) ≠ Nina slog **hende** (she hit her)."
     ],
     "tutora": "contenta"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "morgen and formiddag",
     "texto": [
      "- **morgen**: until 9:30-10 → you say **Godmorgen**.\n- **formiddag**: from 10 to 12 → you say **Goddag** already.\n- **eftermiddag**: the afternoon."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
